        unknown_when: "no altitude sent",
        out_of_window: "outside the alarm's altitude window" %>

  <div class="feature">
    <div>
      <h3 id="nearby">Who is out there, <span class="highlight">nearest first</span>.</h3>
      <p>
        The radar says where to look. This page says who is there. One row per
        aircraft with a known position: its callsign if it broadcasts one and its
        radio address otherwise, the horizontal distance between you, and how far above or
        below you it is, or two dashes when it sends no altitude. On the top
        line, your own callsign with the radio address you transmit under beside it,
        and the count of every aircraft heard.
      </p>
      <p>
        The letter at the start of the row tells you where the information came from.
        <span class="mono">A</span> for an ADS-L message received directly,
        <span class="mono">F</span> for FLARM-compatible traffic,
        <span class="mono">U</span> for an aircraft relayed by a ground station.
      </p>
    </div>
    <figure class="shot">
      <%= screen_image_tag "nearby.png", alt: "The nearby page: your own callsign S-BLIP with its radio address beside it and the count of every aircraft heard on the top line, then five aircraft listed nearest first, each with a letter showing the source of the information, its callsign or radio address, its horizontal distance and its altitude relative to you" %>
      <figcaption>Nearby</figcaption>
    </figure>
  </div>
</section>

